From: FlipperEmu
Subject: [PATCH] hw/sd/sd: SPI mode: enter transfer state when ACMD41 completes

In SPI mode the card only reached sd_transfer_state through CMD9/CMD10
(spi_cmd_SEND_CxD). Hosts that read a block right after ACMD41/CMD58/CMD16
- the Flipper Zero firmware does - got 'CMD16/CMD17 in a wrong state:
ready'. The SD spec has no identification or stand-by phase in SPI mode:
keep reporting In-Idle-State until power-up completes, then accept data
transfer commands.

Signed-off-by: FlipperEmu
---
--- a/hw/sd/sd.c
+++ b/hw/sd/sd.c
@@ -2297,7 +2297,14 @@
     }
 
     if (sd_is_spi(sd)) {
-        sd->state = sd_ready_state;
+        /*
+         * SPI mode has no identification/stand-by phase: R1 reports
+         * "in idle state" until power-up completes, after which the
+         * card accepts data transfer commands straight away.
+         */
+        if (FIELD_EX32(sd->ocr, OCR, CARD_POWER_UP)) {
+            sd->state = sd_transfer_state;
+        }
         return sd_r1;
     } else {
         if (FIELD_EX32(sd->ocr & req.arg, OCR, VDD_VOLTAGE_WINDOW)) {
